# CODEOWNERS — who approves a PR in this repo.
#
# Generated from The Merge Gate §02 (rev 2), the reviewed per-repo merge policy.
# Repo write access does NOT equal merge rights. This file decides who approves.
#
#   lane      auto if clean
#   approvals 1
#   primary   @sidchaudhary
#   backup    — none named yet; see Merge Gate §04 open item 5
#
# This repo has one owner. Under §03 it can never auto-merge — a single owner
# means auto-merge would mean nobody ever reads the code. Naming a backup is
# what changes that, not a policy exception.
#
# The repository is public and accepts external contributions. A contributor's
# recipe is executed by an agent inside customer projects, so every pull request
# is reviewed by an owner for safety, not only for quality. Write access is not
# merge rights and forks cannot approve themselves.

# Default owner for every path.
*                       @sidchaudhary

# CI and release surface. Changing what runs on merge changes the gate itself,
# so it is listed explicitly rather than inherited from the default line.
/.github/               @sidchaudhary

# The licence and the contribution terms. Changing these changes what a
# contributor has agreed to, so they never ride along in a recipe PR.
/LICENSE                @sidchaudhary
/README.md              @sidchaudhary

# The authoring skill is the contract contributors are told to follow.
/.claude/               @sidchaudhary

